- Which Config rules would you add beyond public access and encryption?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, secure cross-account access with ephemeral credentials, tenant isolation, and proactive breach testing in a real-world multi-account data pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Roles Anywhere + OIDC for short-lived, tenant-scoped credentials
- Lake Formation per-tenant access controls
- Cross-account trust with least privilege
- CMK rotation and key policy governance
- Automated breach simulations, revocation, comprehensive auditing

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "kinesis:DescribeStream",
        "kinesis:GetRecords",
        "kinesis:GetShardIterator"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kinesis:account-a:region:stream/tenant-*-stream",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/TenantID": "${aws:username}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time detection and automated containment of credential abuse in a multi-account CI/CD setup using OIDC tokens.

## Key Concepts
- OIDC-based cross-account access and trust policies
- Real-time threat detection: CloudTrail, Security Hub, IAM Access Analyzer
- Containment automation: credential rotation, trust policy adjustments, resource quarantine
- Automation tooling: EventBridge, Step Functions, Secrets Manager

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: IAM trust policy snippet with OIDC
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub": "repo:org/repo:ref:refs/heads/main"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment playbook?
- Which logs and metrics confirm rollback reliability and minimal pipeline disruption?
